      "Wind the wire forward in evenly spaced open spirals, five to seven turns depending on hook size, and lock it with two tight thread turns behind the bead.",
      "Break the wire off by waggling it back and forth (helicoptering) rather than cutting, which leaves no stub to catch tippet.",
      "Optionally dub a tiny collar of UV Black Ice Dub behind the bead, then build a small thread collar, whip finish behind the bead and cut the thread.",
      "A drop of head cement on the collar is optional; the wire rib already protects the body.",
