      "Stack a small bunch of white calf tail and tie it in at the bend as a tail about one shank length long. Bind the butts forward to keep the body smooth.",
      "Tie two strands of white rubber across the top of the shank just ahead of the middle with figure-eight wraps so they form an X with a leg on each corner.",
      "Tie in the chenille at the bend and wrap it forward, passing it around the legs so they stay separated in their X, to a short distance behind the eye. Tie off and trim.",
      "Cut and stack a bunch of deer body hair. Tie it in behind the eye with the tips pointing back over the body so it lies flat as a low wing or shellback reaching to about the tail; take the wraps firm but not so tight the hair flares upright.",
      "Cross the thread over the hair butts in an X to pin the wing down and shape the small shellback, then trim the butts.",
