      "Craven undersizes the hackle and often clips the bottom flush for a low posture; Tightline's Tim Flagler stresses stripping the hackle stem properly so it does not roll as you palmer it.",
      "MidCurrent's advice: 12-15 ft leaders with 6X or 7X, dead-drift in slow water, and hang it behind a bigger dry when you cannot see it.",
