      "Andrew Guibord fishes his string leech on the swing through winter runs, wading down step by step; he calls it a fly for patient, deliberate coverage.",
      "Variants: Black/purple swaps in a purple collar or a purple strip over black. Silvey's Tail Light is Brian Silvey's two-tube Idylwilde version, an offspring of his Tandem Tube, in which a tiny rear tube pins the end of the long bunny strip; rig it with an oversized loop knot and a Gamakatsu Octopus 1 to 4. Larimer's Reverse Marabou is Tom Larimer's tube fly with the marabou tied backwards so the fibres flare forward under tension, giving a big profile from little material that still sinks fast; the Deneki tie uses blue over black blood-quill marabou, a UV polar chenille ball, black and blue Flashabou, a schlappen collar and a fluorescent orange tube cone.",
