      "Wind a smooth thread base forward over the butts to about two-thirds up the shank. Tie in the tinsel (and rib wire if you use one) there, wind the tinsel back to the tail in touching turns and forward again over itself, then tie off and trim. If you added wire, spiral it forward now.",
